.Dd June 14, 2026
.Dt MBT_TRACKER 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_tracker_udp_announce ,
.Nm mbt_tracker_http_announce ,
.Nm mbt_tracker_announce ,
.Nm mbt_tracker_group_new ,
.Nm mbt_tracker_group_free
.Nd Tracker announcement client functions for BitTorrent.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/tracker.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_tracker_udp_announce "const char *url" "struct mbt_tracker_request *req"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_tracker_http_announce "const char *url" "struct mbt_tracker_request *req" "mbt_http_fn http" "void *http_arg"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_tracker_announce "const char *url" "struct mbt_tracker_request *req" "mbt_http_fn http" "void *http_arg"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_tracker_group_new "struct mbt_tracker_group **out"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_tracker_group_free "struct mbt_tracker_group *g"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm mbt_tracker
library provides functions to announce torrent progress to trackers using the UDP (BEP 15) and HTTP (BEP 3) protocols.
All functions provided are asynchronous or rely on callbacks to notify when an announcement is completed or an error occurs.
.Sh STRUCTURES AND CALLBACKS
The primary structure used in these functions is
.Vt mbt_tracker_request
.Pp
This structure contains the necessary context for the announcement, including:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Vt ev
The event loop to which the request is attached.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Vt ih
A pointer to the Torrent infohash.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Vt peer_id
The 20-byte peer identifier.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Vt listen_port
The port the peer is listening on.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Vt ip
The address to report to the tracker, or
.Dv NULL .
An HTTP announce sends it as the
.Ar ip
parameter.
A UDP announce sends an IPv4 address in the IP field, and no IPv6 address.
The tracker can ignore it.
The string is read during the call.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Vt peer_cb
A callback invoked for each peer returned by the tracker.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Vt done_cb
A callback invoked when the announcement completes or fails.
.El
.Sh FUNCTIONS
The following functions perform the announcements:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_tracker_group_new
Makes a group. Set
.Fa group
in a request to add its UDP announce to the group.
.It .Fn mbt_tracker_group_free
Drops pending UDP announces of the group, with no callback.
Free the group before the state that the callbacks use.
.It .Fn mbt_tracker_udp_announce
Performs an asynchronous UDP tracker announcement (BEP 15). The function returns 0 if the request was successfully initiated, or a negative error code on failure.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_tracker_http_announce
Performs an HTTP tracker announcement (BEP 3). This function requires an implementation of the
.Vt mbt_http_fn
callback to handle the underlying HTTP transport. It returns 0 on success or a negative error code on failure.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_tracker_announce
A dispatcher function that selects between UDP and HTTP announcement based on the scheme provided in the
.Vt url.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt 3
